ROLE: You make literal edits to two TypeScript files. Re-read each first. Make exactly these edits and nothing else.

CONTEXT: In `.skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime/src/runtime/client.ts`, `close()` sends SIGTERM to an in-flight provisioning subprocess and returns at once. A subprocess that ignores SIGTERM outlives the client. The runtime child is already handled with a wait for exit plus a SIGKILL after 2 seconds; provisioning should get the same.

ACTION:

1. In `client.ts`, inside `async close()`, replace these two lines:

    this.closed = true;
    this.provisioning?.kill("SIGTERM");

with:

    this.closed = true;
    const provisioning = this.provisioning;
    if (provisioning && provisioning.exitCode === null && provisioning.signalCode === null) {
      provisioning.kill("SIGTERM");
      const escalate = setTimeout(() => provisioning.kill("SIGKILL"), 2_000);
      await once(provisioning, "exit").catch(() => undefined).then(() => clearTimeout(escalate));
    }

2. In `.skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime/src/runtime/client.test.ts`, directly before the final line `});` of the file (the line that closes `describe("RuntimeClient close", () => {`), insert this test:

  it("forces a provisioning step that ignores SIGTERM to exit before close resolves", async () => {
    const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), "sk-vision-client-"));
    const pidFile = join(dir, "uv.pid");
    const fakeUv = join(dir, "uv");
    writeFileSync(fakeUv, `#!/bin/sh\ntrap '' TERM\necho $$ > "${pidFile}"\nwhile :; do sleep 1; done\n`);
    chmodSync(fakeUv, 0o755);

    const saved = {
      uv: process.env.SK_VISION_UV,
      venv: process.env.SK_VISION_VENV_DIR,
      python: process.env.SK_VISION_PYTHON,
    };
    process.env.SK_VISION_UV = fakeUv;
    process.env.SK_VISION_VENV_DIR = join(dir, "venv");
    delete process.env.SK_VISION_PYTHON;
    const proto = RuntimeClient.prototype as unknown as {
      hasMoondream(python: string): Promise<boolean>;
      hasUv(): Promise<boolean>;
    };
    const moondream = spyOn(proto, "hasMoondream").mockImplementation(async () => false);
    const uv = spyOn(proto, "hasUv").mockImplementation(async () => true);

    try {
      const client = new RuntimeClient({ pythonPath: join(dir, "missing-python"), timeoutMs: 1_000 });
      for (let i = 0; i < 100 && !existsSync(pidFile); i++) {
        await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 20));
      }
      expect(existsSync(pidFile)).toBe(true);
      const pid = Number(readFileSync(pidFile, "utf8").trim());

      await client.close();
      let alive = true;
      try {
        process.kill(pid, 0);
      } catch {
        alive = false;
      }
      expect(alive).toBe(false);
      await Promise.race([
        client.ready,
        new Promise((_, reject) => setTimeout(() => reject(new Error("ready did not settle")), 2_000)),
      ]);
    } finally {
      moondream.mockRestore();
      uv.mockRestore();
      for (const [key, value] of [
        ["SK_VISION_UV", saved.uv],
        ["SK_VISION_VENV_DIR", saved.venv],
        ["SK_VISION_PYTHON", saved.python],
      ] as const) {
        if (value === undefined) delete process.env[key];
        else process.env[key] = value;
      }
    }
  }, 10_000);

FORMAT: Then run `cd .skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime && bunx tsc --noEmit; echo typecheck-exit=$?; bun test src/runtime/client.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -5` and print the output verbatim, nothing else.
